710
00:51:22.385 --> 00:51:24.305
Sync throughput is about pipelining:

711
00:51:24.585 --> 00:51:35.167
Waiting for each 20-document task to finish capped the indexer below the write rate, so lag grew to 22 s (p50) / 43 s (p99).

712
00:51:35.447 --> 00:51:47.116
Enqueuing and moving on (the engine auto-batches queued tasks) kept lag at ~0.8 s or 1.1 s, whether batches held 20 or 500 documents.

713
00:51:47.396 --> 00:51:51.471
The same is true of Elasticsearch bulk requests and refresh intervals.

714
00:51:52.821 --> 00:51:53.503
