726
00:53:02.107 --> 00:53:13.478
The embeddings in Part B are a toy: hand-written concept vectors per product type (breakfast, dairy, snack, protein...) with a small keyword, then concept lexicon for queries.

727
00:53:13.758 --> 00:53:18.729
They stand in for a learned model (a multilingual sentence-embedding model in production).

728
00:53:19.009 --> 00:53:23.126
The point is how the retrievers fail differently, not the absolute numbers.

