767
00:59:31.779 --> 00:59:33.059
Production Concerns.

768
00:59:34.309 --> 00:59:35.461
Failure modes.

769
00:59:35.741 --> 00:59:37.085
Here is a quick table:

770
00:59:37.365 --> 00:59:40.352
Failure, and Symptom, and Cause, and Mitigation.

771
00:59:40.632 --> 00:59:42.573
Zero results for common intents.

772
00:59:42.853 --> 00:59:43.664
Symptom:

773
00:59:43.944 --> 00:59:46.376
High zero-result rate, lost orders.

774
00:59:46.656 --> 00:59:47.424
Cause:

775
00:59:47.704 --> 00:59:51.480
No transliteration or synonyms, vocabulary mismatch.

776
00:59:51.760 --> 00:59:52.763
Mitigation:

777
00:59:53.043 --> 00:59:58.397
Analyzer stages (L1), aliases (L3), weekly zero-result review.

778
00:59:58.677 --> 01:00:01.323
Relevance regression after a config change.

779
01:00:01.603 --> 01:00:02.413
Symptom:

780
01:00:02.693 --> 01:00:04.507
CTR drops, complaints.

781
01:00:04.787 --> 01:00:05.555
Cause:

782
01:00:05.835 --> 01:00:10.549
Untested synonym or boost or fuzzy change (L1: fuzzy broke chai).

783
01:00:10.829 --> 01:00:11.832
Mitigation:

784
01:00:12.112 --> 01:00:15.440
Judged-query CI, staged rollout, config in Git.

785
01:00:15.720 --> 01:00:17.107
Out-of-stock at the top.

786
01:00:17.387 --> 01:00:18.197
Symptom:

787
01:00:18.477 --> 01:00:19.629
Low add-to-cart.

788
01:00:19.909 --> 01:00:20.677
Cause:

789
01:00:20.957 --> 01:00:22.835
Ranking ignores availability.

790
01:00:23.115 --> 01:00:24.117
Mitigation:

791
01:00:24.397 --> 01:00:27.768
Stock filter or demotion at query time (L1 C).

792
01:00:28.048 --> 01:00:29.029
Index lag.

793
01:00:29.309 --> 01:00:30.120
Symptom:

794
01:00:30.400 --> 01:00:32.469
Old prices or stock in results.

795
01:00:32.749 --> 01:00:33.517
Cause:

796
01:00:33.797 --> 01:00:38.107
Indexer synchronous per request, bulk too small, refresh too frequent.

797
01:00:38.387 --> 01:00:39.389
Mitigation:

798
01:00:39.669 --> 01:00:41.845
Pipelining, bulk sizing (L3:

799
01:00:42.125 --> 01:00:45.581
22 s, then 0.8 s), refresh interval.

800
01:00:46.931 --> 01:00:48.190
Stale documents.

801
01:00:48.470 --> 01:00:49.281
Symptom:

802
01:00:49.561 --> 01:00:51.950
Index disagrees with DB permanently.

803
01:00:52.230 --> 01:00:52.998
Cause:

804
01:00:53.278 --> 01:00:55.113
Out-of-order updates (L3:

805
01:00:55.393 --> 01:00:57.697
26 regressions), lost deletes.

806
01:00:57.977 --> 01:00:58.979
Mitigation:

807
01:00:59.259 --> 01:01:04.593
Key-partitioned stream, external versions, tombstones, periodic reconciliation.

808
01:01:04.873 --> 01:01:06.025
Reindex outage.

809
01:01:06.305 --> 01:01:07.115
Symptom:

810
01:01:07.395 --> 01:01:09.102
Empty results during rebuild.

811
01:01:09.382 --> 01:01:10.150
Cause:

812
01:01:10.430 --> 01:01:11.582
In-place rebuild.

813
01:01:11.862 --> 01:01:12.865
Mitigation:

814
01:01:13.145 --> 01:01:15.726
Build new index + alias swap (L3:

815
01:01:16.006 --> 01:01:17.094
0 errors).

816
01:01:17.374 --> 01:01:19.337
Hot shard or GC pauses.

817
01:01:19.617 --> 01:01:22.198
Symptom: p99 spikes during sales.

818
01:01:22.478 --> 01:01:23.246
Cause:

819
01:01:23.526 --> 01:01:27.195
Large shards, deep pagination, expensive aggregations.

820
01:01:27.475 --> 01:01:28.478
Mitigation:

821
01:01:28.758 --> 01:01:34.177
Shard sizing (10 to 50 GB), searchafter instead of deep from, circuit breakers.

822
01:01:34.457 --> 01:01:36.611
ANN recall collapse with filters.

823
01:01:36.891 --> 01:01:37.702
Symptom:

824
01:01:37.982 --> 01:01:40.819
Few or wrong results for filtered vector queries.

825
01:01:41.099 --> 01:01:41.867
Cause:

826
01:01:42.147 --> 01:01:45.454
Pre-filtering breaks HNSW graph connectivity.

827
01:01:45.734 --> 01:01:46.737
Mitigation:

828
01:01:47.017 --> 01:01:52.393
Engine's filtered-ANN mode; fall back to exact search for highly selective filters.

829
01:01:53.743 --> 01:01:54.745
Query-of-death.

830
01:01:55.025 --> 01:01:55.836
Symptom:

831
01:01:56.116 --> 01:01:57.908
Cluster CPU saturates.

832
01:01:58.188 --> 01:01:58.956
Cause:

833
01:01:59.236 --> 01:02:02.500
Leading wildcards, huge OR expansions, regexes.

834
01:02:02.780 --> 01:02:03.783
Mitigation:

835
01:02:04.063 --> 01:02:08.329
Query validation, disallow leading wildcards, limits on expansion.

836
01:02:09.679 --> 01:02:10.767
Observability.

837
01:02:11.047 --> 01:02:25.277
Quality: zero-result rate (by script or language, by city), CTR@k, add-to-cart per search, reformulation rate, nDCG on the judged set per deploy, top zero-result queries (a daily report).

838
01:02:25.557 --> 01:02:36.458
Latency: p50 or p99 for search and autocomplete; engine-side took-time versus service-side total (network, re-ranking, inventory lookups).

839
01:02:36.738 --> 01:02:48.258
Indexing: end-to-end lag (commit, then searchable), bulk rejections, version conflicts (a proxy for out-of-order events), document count versus source count (reconciliation).

840
01:02:49.608 --> 01:02:55.539
Engine health: heap, GC, segment count, merge throttling, query cache hit rates, shard balance.

841
01:02:56.889 --> 01:02:57.827
Security.

842
01:02:58.107 --> 01:03:00.198
Treat queries as untrusted input.

843
01:03:00.478 --> 01:03:06.323
Build queries with the client's typed API, never by concatenating a query DSL string.

844
01:03:06.603 --> 01:03:11.105
Disallow scripting and leading wildcards, and cap query length and expansions.

845
01:03:11.385 --> 01:03:21.411
Document-level security: customers must never see unpublished products, other sellers' drafts or restricted items (age-restricted, region-restricted).

846
01:03:21.691 --> 01:03:25.403
Use filters applied server-side, not client-provided ones.

847
01:03:25.683 --> 01:03:28.051
Don't index PII into product search.

848
01:03:28.331 --> 01:03:37.377
Back-office search over customers or orders is a separate, access-controlled index with audit logging (Ch 23, Ch 36).

849
01:03:38.727 --> 01:03:44.337
Logs: search queries can contain personal data (names, phone numbers typed into the box).

850
01:03:44.617 --> 01:03:47.860
Redact before storing query logs, and set retention.

851
01:03:49.210 --> 01:03:50.874
Performance and tuning knobs.

852
01:03:51.154 --> 01:03:52.498
Here is a quick table:

853
01:03:52.778 --> 01:03:53.994
Knob, and Guidance.

854
01:03:54.274 --> 01:03:55.341
Shard size:

855
01:03:55.621 --> 01:04:01.146
10 to 50 GB per shard; shards times replicas sized to QPS and data.

856
01:04:01.426 --> 01:04:02.493
Refresh interval:

857
01:04:02.773 --> 01:04:08.533
1 s default; raise during bulk loads (or -1), lower only if the product needs it.

858
01:04:08.813 --> 01:04:09.794
Bulk size:

859
01:04:10.074 --> 01:04:14.618
5 to 15 MB per request; pipeline several in flight (L3).

860
01:04:14.898 --> 01:04:15.751
Fuzziness:

861
01:04:16.031 --> 01:04:21.322
AUTO:5,8 style; prefixlength 1 to 2; max expansions at most 50.

862
01:04:21.602 --> 01:04:22.626
Result window:

863
01:04:22.906 --> 01:04:27.279
Avoid deep from; use searchafter or scroll or PIT for exports.

864
01:04:27.559 --> 01:04:28.455
Filters:

865
01:04:28.735 --> 01:04:32.405
Put exact constraints in filter context (cached, not scored).

866
01:04:32.685 --> 01:04:33.645
Re-ranking:

867
01:04:33.925 --> 01:04:39.087
Re-rank only the top 100 to 1,000 with expensive features or models.

868
01:04:39.367 --> 01:04:40.605
HNSW:

869
01:04:40.885 --> 01:04:49.418
M 16 to 32, efConstruction 100 to 200, efSearch tuned to recall target (L4); quantise for memory.

870
01:04:50.768 --> 01:04:51.835
Autocomplete:

871
01:04:52.115 --> 01:04:58.088
Client debounce 100 to 150 ms, prefix cache, a dedicated lightweight index.

872
01:04:59.438 --> 01:05:00.163
Cost.

873
01:05:00.443 --> 01:05:07.270
Search clusters are memory-hungry (heap + OS page cache for segments), and vector fields multiply that.

874
01:05:07.550 --> 01:05:15.059
Quantisation and dimension choice (384 versus 1,536) are cost decisions.

875
01:05:15.339 --> 01:05:17.451
Replicas cost the same as primaries.

876
01:05:17.731 --> 01:05:21.443
Scale replicas for QPS and primaries for data size.

877
01:05:21.723 --> 01:05:27.569
The cheapest relevance gains in this chapter came from data: aliases, synonyms, a type field.

878
01:05:27.849 --> 01:05:30.601
They cost merchandising hours, not machines.

879
01:05:31.951 --> 01:05:32.889
