01:09:03.659 --> 01:09:04.683
Question 1.

933
01:09:04.963 --> 01:09:06.499
What is an inverted index?

934
01:09:06.779 --> 01:09:08.145
Thirty-second answer:

935
01:09:08.425 --> 01:09:15.849
A map from each term to the list of documents that contain it (a postings list), often with term frequencies and positions.

936
01:09:16.129 --> 01:09:22.017
To search, you look up each query term's postings and combine them, instead of scanning every document.

937
01:09:22.297 --> 01:09:27.182
It's how search engines answer queries over millions of documents in milliseconds.

938
01:09:28.532 --> 01:09:29.535
Question 2.

939
01:09:29.815 --> 01:09:32.097
What is an analyzer, and why does it matter?

940
01:09:32.377 --> 01:09:33.743
Thirty-second answer:

941
01:09:34.023 --> 01:09:44.881
The pipeline that turns text into index terms: normalise characters, split into tokens, then filter (lowercase, stem, synonyms, remove stop words, transliterate).

942
01:09:45.161 --> 01:09:51.903
The same analysis must happen to documents at index time and to queries at search time, or they won't match.

943
01:09:52.183 --> 01:09:54.615
It's the biggest single lever on search quality.

944
01:09:55.965 --> 01:09:57.010
Question 3.

945
01:09:57.290 --> 01:09:58.911
What is BM25?

946
01:09:59.191 --> 01:10:00.557
Thirty-second answer:

947
01:10:00.837 --> 01:10:03.973
The standard relevance-scoring function in search engines.

948
01:10:04.253 --> 01:10:06.045
It scores a document higher when:

949
01:10:07.395 --> 01:10:08.461
Question 4.

950
01:10:08.741 --> 01:10:09.808
What are facets?

951
01:10:10.088 --> 01:10:11.453
Thirty-second answer:

952
01:10:11.733 --> 01:10:20.821
Counts of results per attribute value for the current query, such as Masala 1,022, Snacks 240 or brand and price bands.

953
01:10:21.101 --> 01:10:24.216
They're shown as filters so customers can narrow down.

954
01:10:24.496 --> 01:10:29.552
They're computed from columnar doc values in the engine, or with GROUP BY in SQL.

955
01:10:30.902 --> 01:10:31.905
Intermediate.

