959
01:10:40.153 --> 01:10:43.225
How do you keep a search index in sync with the database?

960
01:10:43.505 --> 01:10:44.871
Thirty-second answer:

961
01:10:45.151 --> 01:10:47.561
Treat the index as a derived read model.

962
01:10:47.841 --> 01:10:51.831
The service writes the entity and an outbox row in one transaction.

963
01:10:52.111 --> 01:10:57.103
CDC or a relay publishes events to Kafka keyed by product id.

964
01:10:57.383 --> 01:11:07.388
An indexer consumes them and sends bulk upserts or deletes to the engine, preserving per-product order (or using external versions so older writes are rejected).

965
01:11:07.668 --> 01:11:15.028
A periodic reconciliation compares counts and checksums, and full rebuilds go to a new index behind an alias.

966
